doc:sch-1-sec-94s-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "94S(2) Breach of requirement may be treated as an eligible data breach" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this Act, if:  (a) a State or Territory health authority; or  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020 No. 44, 2020  (b) person employed by, or in the service of, the State or Territory health authority; breaches a requirement of this Part in relation to COVID app data:  (c) the breach is taken to be an eligible data breach by the State or Territory health authority; and  (d) an individual to whom the data relates is taken to be at risk from the eligible data breach." ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94s-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94S(3) Breach of requirement may be treated as an eligible data breach"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-94s-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Part IIIC applies in relation to such a breach as if:  (a) subsection 26WE(3) and sections 26WF, 26WH and 26WJ did not apply in relation to the breach; and  (b) Subdivision B of Division 3 of that Part:  (i) required the data store administrator, or State or Territory health authority, to notify the Commissioner that there were reasonable grounds to believe that there had been an eligible data breach; and  (ii) only required compliance with sections 26WK and 26WL in relation to the breach if the Commissioner required the administrator or authority so to comply; and  (c) sections 26WN, 26WP, 26WQ, 26WS and 26WT did not apply in relation to the breach." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Part IIIC applies in relation to such a breach as if:  (a) subsection 26WE(3) and sections 26WF, 26WH and 26WJ did not apply in relation to the breach; and  (b) Subdivision B of Division 3 of that Part:  (i) required the data store administrator, or State or Territory health authority, to notify the Commissioner that there were reasonable grounds to believe that there had been an eligible data breach; and  (ii) only required compliance with sections 26WK and 26WL in relation to the breach if the Commissioner required the administrator or authority so to comply; and  (c) sections 26WN, 26WP, 26WQ, 26WS and 26WT did not apply in relation to the breach."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6ee55c9d1b121e1475a109941ae250962b3bff6d2614399752fa170f9fe3691d" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94s ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notify the Commissioner of reasonable grounds to believe an eligible data breach has occurred." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf> ;
