concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94u-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94U(4) Investigation under section 40 to cease if COVID data offence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-94u-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Commissioner of Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions:  (a) has been informed of the Commissioner’s opinion under paragraph (2)(a); and  (b) is satisfied that an investigation relating to the matter, or proceedings for an offence relating to the matter, will not be jeopardised, or otherwise affected, by continuation of the Commissioner’s investigation; the Commissioner of Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions, as the case requires, may give a written notice to that effect to the Commissioner." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the Commissioner of Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions:  (a) has been informed of the Commissioner’s opinion under paragraph (2)(a); and  (b) is satisfied that an investigation relating to the matter, or proceedings for an offence relating to the matter, will not be jeopardised, or otherwise affected, by continuation of the Commissioner’s investigation; the Commissioner of Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions, as the case requires, may give a written notice to that effect to the Commissioner."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "632eaf29af77a3e9fcdd6d77e79fc23efd68f287b959ddbf9189af1ec1a1c327" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94u ;
