    skos:definition "(1) If:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 44, 2020 Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020  (a) a complaint has been made under section 36 about an act or practice that may involve a breach of a requirement of this Part; and  (b) before the Commissioner commences, or after the Commissioner has commenced, to investigate the matter, the Commissioner forms the opinion that:  (i) the complainant has made, or could have made, a complaint relating to that matter to a State or Territory privacy authority; and  (ii) that matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt with by that State or Territory authority; the Commissioner may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to investigate the matter further."@en ;
