    cml:operator "Analyze" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Analysis of investigation and referral to State/Territory authority" ;
    cml:premiseText "(a) a complaint has been made under section 36..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Investigation and referral analyzed." ;
    cml:executionSurface "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-94v-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "94V(1) Referring COVID data matters to State or Territory privacy" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 44, 2020 Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020  (a) a complaint has been made under section 36 about an act or practice that may involve a breach of a requirement of this Part; and  (b) before the Commissioner commences, or after the Commissioner has commenced, to investigate the matter, the Commissioner forms the opinion that:  (i) the complainant has made, or could have made, a complaint relating to that matter to a State or Territory privacy authority; and  (ii) that matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt with by that State or Territory authority; the Commissioner may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to investigate the matter further." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94V(2) Referring COVID data matters to State or Territory privacy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-94v-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the Commissioner so decides, the Commissioner must:  (a) transfer the complaint to that State or Territory authority; and  (b) give notice in writing to the complainant stating that the complaint has been so transferred; and  (c) give to that State or Territory authority any information or documents that relate to the complaint and are in the possession, or under the control, of the Commissioner." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the Commissioner so decides, the Commissioner must:  (a) transfer the complaint to that State or Territory authority; and  (b) give notice in writing to the complainant stating that the complaint has been so transferred; and  (c) give to that State or Territory authority any information or documents that relate to the complaint and are in the possession, or under the control, of the Commissioner."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4bf33c7b58408c409102e533dc850b4d208ed024df01e47ce07d960a4aa351d0" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94v ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Transfer complaint to State or Territory authority and provide notice." ;
    dc:description "Notice in writing to the complainant stating that the complaint has been transferred." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
