concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94ZA Reports on operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-94za ;
    values:originalText "National COVIDSafe Data Store  (1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:  (a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part; and  (b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting on or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020 No. 44, 2020  cause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6 month period. Note: Section 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report. It would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under subsection 94D(2).  (2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report under subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be prepared within 3 months after that day.  (3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the preparation of the report." ;
    skos:definition "National COVIDSafe Data Store  (1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:  (a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part; and  (b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting on or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020 No. 44, 2020  cause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6 month period. Note: Section 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report. It would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under subsection 94D(2).  (2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report under subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be prepared within 3 months after that day.  (3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the preparation of the report."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41ec30cdf725a17bffa428994ae0a79d6406794343ba7cc7afbc5e6bbe500138" ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020-sch-1-sec-94za-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf> ;
    dc:source "privacy-amendment-public-health-contact-information-act-2020.pdf, p.25" .
doc:sch-1-sec-94za a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "94ZA Reports on operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "National COVIDSafe Data Store  (1) The Health Minister must, as soon as practicable after:  (a) the end of the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part; and  (b) the end of each subsequent 6 month period (if any) starting on or before the day determined under subsection 94Y(1);  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Public Health Contact Information) Act 2020 No. 44, 2020  cause a report to be prepared on the operation and effectiveness of COVIDSafe and the National COVIDSafe Data Store during that 6 month period. Note: Section 94D prevents the inclusion of COVID app data in the report. It would not be a permitted collection, use or disclosure under subsection 94D(2).  (2) If the day determined under subsection 94Y(1) occurs during the 6 month period starting on the commencement of this Part, the report under subsection (1) of this section relating to that period must be prepared within 3 months after that day.  (3) The Health Minister must cause copies of a report prepared under subsection (1) to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the completion of the preparation of the report." ;
    cof:pageNumber "25"^^xsd:integer .

